WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.000
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.559
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:16.586
Unit seventeen: Cloze Test Strategies. Today you will complete a text by choosing the right word for each gap.

4
00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:19.562
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.942
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.633
Cloze.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.998
Cloze means a text with missing words.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.014
Do the cloze test.

9
00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:34.095
Your turn. Say: Cloze.

10
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:37.865
Cloze.

11
00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:39.432
Gap.

12
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.929
Gap means a missing word.

13
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:43.622
Fill each gap.

14
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.648
Your turn. Say: Gap.

15
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.013
Gap.

16
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.844
Context.

17
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.360
Context means the words around a gap.

18
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.474
Use the context.

19
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.921
Your turn. Say: Context.

20
00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:04.675
Context.

21
00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:06.302
Grammar.

22
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.525
Grammar means rules for using words.

23
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.292
Check the grammar.

24
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:14.118
Your turn. Say: Grammar.

25
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:18.142
Grammar.

26
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:20.059
Collocation.

27
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.317
Collocation means words that go together.

28
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.870
Make a mistake is a collocation.

29
00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:29.031
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

30
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:32.995
Collocation.

31
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.844
Preposition.

32
00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.604
Preposition means a word like in, on or at.

33
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:40.601
Choose the preposition.

34
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:43.428
Your turn. Say: Preposition.

35
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:47.361
Preposition.

36
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:49.118
Conjunction.

37
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.766
Conjunction means a word that joins ideas.

38
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.711
But is a conjunction.

39
00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:57.690
Your turn. Say: Conjunction.

40
00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:01.558
Conjunction.

41
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:03.097
Option.

42
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.269
Option means one possible answer.

43
00:02:06.883 --> 00:02:08.314
Choose the best option.

44
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:11.035
Your turn. Say: Option.

45
00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.831
Option.

46
00:02:15.633 --> 00:02:19.122
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.983 --> 00:02:22.296
Visal, how do I do a cloze test?

48
00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:34.070
Read the whole text first to understand the topic. Then look at each gap and decide what kind of word is missing: a noun, a verb, a preposition or a conjunction.

49
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:36.753
What clues help me?

50
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:50.766
Look at the words before and after the gap. A preposition often follows a verb, such as interested in, and a conjunction joins two ideas, such as because or but.

51
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.501
How do I check my answer?

52
00:02:54.617 --> 00:03:06.002
Read the sentence again with your answer in the gap. It must be grammatical and make sense. If two options seem possible, choose the one that sounds natural.

53
00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.422
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:14.013
Grammar focus: Strategy: read, predict, check.

55
00:03:14.313 --> 00:03:15.523
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.217 --> 00:03:18.147
I am interested in learning English.

57
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.166
He was tired, but he finished his work.

58
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:27.838
Read the whole text first, predict the type of word for each gap and read each sentence back to check.

59
00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:32.838
Be careful! Don't say: I choose a word without reading the text.

60
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.043
Say: I read the whole text first.

61
00:03:37.343 --> 00:03:38.565
Read first.

62
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:42.216
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.373
Cloze Practice.

64
00:03:44.673 --> 00:03:47.647
Sophy reads a cloze text about a school festival.

65
00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:51.237
The first gap comes after the word interested.

66
00:03:52.233 --> 00:03:54.988
She knows that the missing word is the preposition in.

67
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.370
The second gap needs a conjunction to join two ideas.

68
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.993
She reads the finished text again to check it.

69
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.450
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.317 --> 00:04:10.980
A cloze test has blank.

71
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.130
A, no words. B, pictures. C, missing words.

72
00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.212
The answer is C: missing words.

73
00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.955
Interested blank music.

74
00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:27.061
A, in. B, on. C, at.

75
00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.135
The answer is A: in.

76
00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:35.039
Before answering you should blank.

77
00:04:35.339 --> 00:04:39.027
A, guess. B, read the whole text. C, skip it.

78
00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:45.298
The answer is B: read the whole text.

79
00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.637
But is a blank.

80
00:04:47.937 --> 00:04:51.126
A, noun. B, verb. C, conjunction.

81
00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.887
The answer is C: conjunction.

82
00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.724
What does Sophy do at the end?

83
00:05:00.024 --> 00:05:04.177
A, checks the text. B, goes home. C, sleeps.

84
00:05:07.733 --> 00:05:10.488
The answer is A: checks the text.

85
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.026
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:15.883 --> 00:05:17.894
How do you do a cloze test?

87
00:05:26.683 --> 00:05:28.288
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.588 --> 00:05:41.936
I read the whole text first so that I understand the topic. Then I decide which type of word fits each gap, and I use the words before and after. At the end I read the text again to check my answers.

89
00:05:42.236 --> 00:05:43.945
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:49.824
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: read, predict, check.

91
00:05:50.124 --> 00:05:55.133
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:05:55.433 --> 00:05:58.074
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:58.374 --> 00:06:01.433
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

